{"final":true,"conversation":{"_id":"69a5e34eb379a0a97bd4cda7","user":"69a5e2d7d52cdf53d7ba83b2","conversationId":"b77435de-c55d-491c-b406-f35843741ca3","__v":0,"agent_id":"deepseek__deepseek-coder___DeepSeek Coder","createdAt":"2026-03-02T19:21:50.552Z","endpoint":"deepseek","endpointType":"custom","expiredAt":null,"files":[],"isArchived":false,"maxContextTokens":111514,"max_tokens":4096,"messages":["69a5e34eb379a0a97bd4cda6","69a5e36ab379a0a97bd4cda8"],"model":"deepseek-coder","resendFiles":true,"spec":"deepseek-coder-agent","tags":[],"temperature":0.3,"title":"New Chat","updatedAt":"2026-03-02T19:22:18.256Z"},"title":"New Chat","requestMessage":{"messageId":"4934faa1-2a14-4e6d-9584-d5faaa9220f1","parentMessageId":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000","conversationId":"b77435de-c55d-491c-b406-f35843741ca3","sender":"User","text":"tell me the weather of brasil sao paulo","isCreatedByUser":true,"tokenCount":15},"responseMessage":{"messageId":"1a8b08fd-bf09-4df5-aa66-a7627ac51ad8","conversationId":"b77435de-c55d-491c-b406-f35843741ca3","parentMessageId":"4934faa1-2a14-4e6d-9584-d5faaa9220f1","isCreatedByUser":false,"isEdited":false,"model":"deepseek-coder","sender":"Deepseek","promptTokens":16,"endpoint":"deepseek","text":"","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Of course. Here is the weather information for São Paulo, Brazil.\n\n**Important Note:** São Paulo has a **tropical highland climate** with mild temperatures year-round, but it can change quickly. The city is known for having \"all four seasons in one day.\"\n\n### Current & Forecasted Conditions (General Overview)\n\n*   **Typical Weather (Late May):** You are currently in late autumn, heading into winter.\n    *   **Temperatures:** Mild to cool. Average highs are around **22-24°C (72-75°F)**, and average lows can drop to **13-15°C (55-59°F)**, especially at night and in the early morning.\n    *   **Rainfall:** This is the drier season. While rain is still possible, it's less frequent and intense than in the summer months.\n    *   **Sky:** Often partly cloudy, with a mix of sun and clouds. Mornings can be foggy or overcast.\n\n### What to Expect Right Now & For the Rest of the Week:\n\n*   **Temperature:** Cool mornings and evenings, warming up pleasantly during the afternoon. **Always carry a light jacket or sweater.**\n*   **Rain:** Always a possibility. It's wise to have an umbrella or a raincoat handy.\n*   **Air Quality:** Can vary, but is generally moderate.\n\n### Seasonal Guide for São Paulo:\n\n*   **Summer (Dec-Feb):** Hot, humid, and rainy. Afternoon thunderstorms are very common. Average highs: 28-30°C (82-86°F).\n*   **Autumn (Mar-May):** Temperatures begin to cool, and rain decreases. Very pleasant weather. This is the current season.\n*   **Winter (Jun-Aug):** The coolest and driest season. Temperatures can occasionally dip below 10°C (50°F) at night. Daytime is usually sunny and mild.\n*   **Spring (Sep-Nov):** Temperatures warm up, and rain increases. Weather can be very changeable.\n\n### **For the Most Accurate, Real-Time Information:**\n\nI am an AI and cannot provide live data. For precise forecasts, current temperature, humidity, and rain radar, please check a dedicated weather service.\n\n**Recommended sites:**\n*   **INMET** (Brazilian National Institute of Meteorology - official source): [https://www.inmet.gov.br/](https://www.inmet.gov.br/)\n*   **Climatempo** (Popular Brazilian weather site): [https://www.climatempo.com.br/](https://www.climatempo.com.br/)\n*   **International apps/sites** like AccuWeather, The Weather Channel, or Weather Underground also provide reliable forecasts for São Paulo.\n\n**In summary for today:** Prepare for mild, changeable weather with a chance of rain. **Layer your clothing** to adapt to temperature shifts throughout the day.\n\nEnjoy your time in São Paulo"}],"attachments":[]}}
